// =============================================================================
// niche-languages.mjs (v89) — three more languages nobody else teaches.
//
// WHY THESE THREE. Each has tens of millions of speakers, a diaspora that
// spends its life away from where the language is spoken, and no course on any
// major platform. That combination is the whole reason this app exists.
//
//   MALAYALAM — ~38M speakers in Kerala, and one of the most travelled
//   populations on earth: millions of Malayalis live and work in the Gulf, plus
//   large communities in the US, UK and Australia. A generation of children
//   grow up in Dubai or Doha understanding their parents and answering in
//   English. No Duolingo course.
//
//   TAMIL — ~80M speakers, and one of the world's oldest living literary
//   languages. Sri Lanka, Malaysia, Singapore, South Africa, the UK, Canada.
//   Also no Duolingo course.
//
//   SOMALI — ~20M speakers, and a diaspora concentrated in exactly the places
//   this app can reach: Minneapolis, London, Birmingham, Toronto, Oslo,
//   Stockholm. Written in Latin script since 1972, so no reading barrier at all.
//   No Duolingo course.
//
// WHAT EACH ONE TURNS ON, taught from the first unit rather than buried:
//
//   Malayalam and Tamil both use the ELDER-SIBLING TITLE for people who are not
//   your siblings — chettan/chechi, anna/akka — the same instinct as Tagalog's
//   kuya/ate. Calling an older stranger by their name alone is the mark of an
//   outsider. Both also mark respect by using the plural for one person.
//
//   Somali marks gender on the article, which attaches to the END of the noun,
//   and has a set of greetings that are near-ritual in length.
//
// SCOPE, SAID PLAINLY. Each pack clears the bars the test suite enforces — 120
// words, the beginner-essentials list, a guide, no thin units — and carries an
// example sentence on every word. None has recorded audio or reading passages;
// those are declared in validate-passages.mjs and tracked in RESEARCH.md rather
// than faked.
// =============================================================================

const w = (unit, category, lemma, translit, translation, examples, extra = {}) => ({
  unit, category, lemma, ...(translit ? { translit } : {}), translation,
  difficulty: extra.difficulty ?? 1,
  ...(extra.note ? { note: extra.note } : {}),
  examples,
});

